flowchart TD
    box_0(["Start"])
    box_1{"Does the part meet quality assurance team product<br/>specifications?"}
    box_2["Check product dimensions and inspect for<br/>contamination."]
    box_3["Remove the non conforming parts and reload with a<br/>product batch that meets quality assurance team<br/>specifications."]
    box_4{"Is picking up part from input slide correct?"}
    box_5["Verification: parts must be centred under the vacuum<br/>end effectors and must not be dropped during<br/>transport. See input slide pickup diagnostic (GRAPH<br/>17) if needed."]
    box_6[/"Input slide pickup diagnostic (GRAPH 17)"/]
    box_7{"Is picking up part from reorientation mechanism<br/>correct?"}
    box_8["Verification: parts must be centred under the vacuum<br/>end effectors and must not be dropped during<br/>transport. See reorientation mechanism placement<br/>diagnostic (GRAPH 19) if needed."]
    box_9[/"Reorientation mechanism placement diagnostic (GRAPH<br/>19)"/]
    box_10{"Is the setup of the indexing table correct?"}
    box_11["Verify that there is no play between the setup tool<br/>and the indexing table during mounting (refer to the<br/>part mounting adjustment procedure). Then refer to<br/>the indexing table setup procedure."]
    box_12[/"Indexing table setup procedure"/]
    box_13{"Are there contaminated parts?"}
    box_14["Complete the following checks: 1. Check whether the<br/>vacuum end effectors are contaminated. 2. Check the<br/>vacuum filters for contamination. 3. Check whether<br/>the assembly robot axes are contaminated."]
    box_15[/"Pneumatic flow measurement procedure: vacuum flow<br/>check"/]
    box_16["Clean the parts, replace the vacuum filters, and<br/>replace the vacuum hose."]
    box_17[/"Assembly robot axis lubrication procedure"/]
    box_18{"Are there electrical defects?"}
    box_19["Complete the following checks: 1. Check cabling and<br/>upper displacement sensors on the vacuum end<br/>effectors. 2. Check whether the vacuum switches work<br/>correctly. 3. Check whether the valve for the vacuum<br/>generator works correctly. 4. Check system settings<br/>on the operator control interface."]
    box_20["Replace the defective cabling and/or displacement<br/>sensor on the vacuum end effectors."]
    box_21{"Are there worn parts?"}
    box_22["Complete the following checks: 1. Check wear on the<br/>vacuum end effectors. 2. Check wear on the actuator<br/>grippers. 3. Check wear on the gripper pin through<br/>the aluminium block. 4. Check the assembly robot<br/>axes for wear."]
    box_23["Replace the worn components identified in the<br/>inspection (vacuum end effectors, actuator grippers,<br/>gripper pin, and/or assembly robot axes)."]
    box_24[/"Assembly robot replacement procedure"/]
    box_25{"Is the z parallelism of the lower position of 4x<br/>gripper relative to each other correct?"}
    box_26[/"Refer to the Z parallelism check for variant A<br/>machines (small format parts)."/]
    box_27[/"Refer to the Z parallelism check for variant B<br/>machines (medium format parts)."/]
    box_28[/"Refer to the Z parallelism check for variant C<br/>machines (large format parts)."/]
    box_29["Readjust the Z parallelism of the 4x gripper lower<br/>positions to the specified tolerance."]
    box_30{"Is the part placement position in the indexing table<br/>correct?"}
    box_31[/"Refer to the Z height and XY placement position<br/>check for variant A machines (small format parts)."/]
    box_32[/"Refer to the Z height and XY placement position<br/>check for variant B machines (medium format parts)."/]
    box_33[/"Refer to the Z height and XY placement position<br/>check for variant C machines (large format parts)."/]
    box_34[/"Pick up and placement adjustment procedure: part in<br/>indexing table"/]
    box_35["Perform assembly robot calibrations to correct the Z<br/>height and XY placement position into the indexing<br/>table fixture."]
    box_36["Restart this diagnostic procedure from the<br/>beginning."]
    box_37(["Placing part in indexing table is correct"])

